{"tool_name":"kat","contents":["biocontainers","galaxy","bioschemas","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"kat","version":"2.4.2","home":"https://github.com/TGAC/KAT","documentation":"https://kat.readthedocs.io/en/latest","license":"GPL-3.0-or-later","summary":"KAT is a suite of tools that analyse jellyfish hashes or sequence files (fasta or fastq) using kmer counts.","identifiers":["biotools:kat","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btw663"],"license_file":"COPYING","build":{"number":5,"run_exports":[null],"skip":true},"requirements":{"build":["make",null,"autoconf","automake","libtool","pkg-config"],"host":["python","pip","zlib","numpy","scipy","matplotlib-base","tabulate","boost-cpp <1.84.0"],"run":["python","numpy","scipy","matplotlib-base","tabulate","boost-cpp <1.84.0"]},"source_url":"https://github.com/TGAC/KAT/archive/Release-2.4.2.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["kat --version"]}},"biocontainers":{"name":"kat","identifiers":["biotools:KAT","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btw663"],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"KAT is a suite of tools that analyse jellyfish hashes or sequence files (fasta or fastq) using kmer counts","home_url":"https://github.com/TGAC/KAT","keywords":["Fraxinus","Genome, Plant","High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Quality Control","Sequence Analysis, DNA","Sequence analysis","Genomics"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":7},"biotools":{"id":"kat","home":"http://www.earlham.ac.uk/kat-tools","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Suite of tools that generate, analyse and compare k-mer spectra produced from sequence files","addition_date":"2017-08-20T15:57:35Z","last_update_date":"2019-09-04T08:38:13Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"collections":["Animal and Crop Genomics"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:kat","credit":[{"email":"daniel.mappleson@earlham.ac.uk","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://kat.readthedocs.org/en/latest/"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["animalandcropgenomics"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Sequence composition calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0236"},{"term":"Sequence feature detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0253"}]}],"name":"KAT","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"admin","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btw663","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2017 The Author.Motivation: De novo assembly of whole genome shotgun (WGS) next-generation sequencing (NGS) data benefits from high-quality input with high coverage. However, in practice, determining the quality and quantity of useful reads quickly and in a reference-free manner is not trivial. Gaining a better understanding of the WGS data, and how that data is utilized by assemblers, provides useful insights that can inform the assembly process and result in better assemblies. Results: We present the K-mer Analysis Toolkit (KAT): a multi-purpose software toolkit for reference-free quality control (QC) of WGS reads and de novo genome assemblies, primarily via their k-mer frequencies and GC composition. KAT enables users to assess levels of errors, bias and contamination at various stages of the assembly process. In this paper we highlight KAT's ability to provide valuable insights into assembly composition and quality of genome assemblies through pairwise comparison of k-mers present in both input reads and the assemblies.","authors":[{"name":"Accinelli G.G."},{"name":"Clavijo B.J."},{"name":"Kettleborough G."},{"name":"Mapleson D."},{"name":"Wright J."}],"citationCount":103,"date":"2017-02-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"KAT: A K-mer analysis toolkit to quality control NGS datasets and genome assemblies"},"pmcid":"PMC5408915","pmid":"27797770","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Genomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0622"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"KAT","home